ics. Then learn tools like Excel and SQL for data handling and analysis. After that, move to Python or R for advanced analysis and practice regularly with real-world projects to build strong practical skills.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-learn-data-analytics\/#faq-question-1773829186060","position":4,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-learn-data-analytics\/#faq-question-1773829186060","name":"4. Can a beginner learn data analytics?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, beginners can learn data analytics easily with proper guidance and consistent practice. Starting with basics and gradually learning tools and projects helps build a strong foundation in data analytics.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-learn-data-analytics\/#faq-question-1773829198508","position":5,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-learn-data-analytics\/#faq-question-1773829198508","name":"5. How long does it take to learn data analytics?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It usually takes around 3\u20136 months to learn the basics of data analytics and 6\u201312 months to become job-ready, depending on your learning consistency, practice, and project experience.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-learn-data-analytics\/#faq-question-1773829210960","position":6,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-learn-data-analytics\/#faq-question-1773829210960","name":"6. Is coding required for data analytics?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Coding is not strictly required for beginners, but learning programming languages like Python or R helps perform advanced data analysis, automate tasks, and handle large datasets efficiently.","inLanguage":"en-US"}